      "raw_text": "To determine how many years before the tire needs to be replaced, we need to calculate the total number of rotations the tire will undergo in one year and then compare that to the tire's lifespan.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the number of rotations per mile.**\nThe problem states that every 2 miles, the tires rotate 725 times.\n$$ \\text{Rotations per mile} = \\frac{725 \\text{ rotations}}{2 \\text{ miles}} = 362.5 \\text{ rotations/mile} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total miles driven per year.**\nJeremy drives 400 miles per month. There are 12 months in a year.\n$$ \\text{Miles per year} = 400 \\text{ miles/month} \\times 12 \\text{ months/year} = 4,800 \\text{ miles/year} $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total rotations per year.**\nMultiply the miles driven per year by the rotations per mile.\n$$ \\text{Rotations per year} = 4,800 \\text{ miles} \\times 362.5 \\text{ rotations/mile} $$\n$$ 4,800 \\times 362.5 = 1,740,000 \\text{ rotations/year} $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the number of years until replacement.**\nThe tire can undergo 10,440,000 rotations. Divide the total lifespan rotations by the annual rotations.\n$$ \\text{Years} = \\frac{10,440,000 \\text{ total rotations}}{1,740,000 \\text{ rotations/year}} $$\n$$ \\text{Years} = \\frac{1044}{174} $$\n$$ \\text{Years} = 6 $$\n\nThe tire will need to be replaced after 6 years.\n\n#### 6<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To determine how many years before the tire needs to be replaced, we need to calculate the total number of rotations the tire will undergo in one year and then compare that to the tire's lifespan.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the number of rotations per mile.**\nThe problem states that every 2 miles, the tires rotate 725 times.\n$$ \\text{Rotations per mile} = \\frac{725 \\text{ rotations}}{2 \\text{ miles}} = 362.5 \\text{ rotations/mile} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total miles driven per year.**\nJeremy drives 400 miles per month. There are 12 months in a year.\n$$ \\text{Miles per year} = 400 \\text{ miles/month} \\times 12 \\text{ months/year} = 4,800 \\text{ miles/year} $$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total rotations per year.**\nMultiply the miles driven per year by the rotations per mile.\n$$ \\text{Rotations per year} = 4,800 \\text{ miles} \\times 362.5 \\text{ rotations/mile} $$\n$$ 4,800 \\times 362.5 = 1,740,000 \\text{ rotations/year} $$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the number of years until replacement.**\nThe tire can undergo 10,440,000 rotations. Divide the total lifespan rotations by the annual rotations.\n$$ \\text{Years} = \\frac{10,440,000 \\text{ total rotations}}{1,740,000 \\text{ rotations/year}} $$\n$$ \\text{Years} = \\frac{1044}{174} $$\n$$ \\text{Years} = 6 $$\n\nThe tire will need to be replaced after 6 years.\n\n#### 6",
      "input_sha256": "4dfe0fd186d5d312506f58c9a48948a9ad12a23752b693b35069aedfe53e19f4",
      "parsed_answer": "6",
